,1106,1107],{},"Each isolate has a debug name (for debugging\u002Fprofiling).",[23,1109,1111],{"id":1110},"limitations","Limitations",[39,1113,1114,1123,1129],{},[42,1115,1116,1119,1120,1122],{},[18,1117,1118],{},"Web",": isolates don't exist on the web (Dart compiles to JS, which is single-threaded with Web Workers as a partial analog). ",[31,1121,59],{}," throws on web, or falls back to running on the main thread (depending on the setup).",[42,1124,1125,1128],{},[18,1126,1127],{},"Spawn overhead",": ~50ms to spawn an isolate. For many small tasks, a worker pool is better (spawn once, send many messages).",[42,1130,1131,1134],{},[18,1132,1133],{},"No shared memory",": isolates can't share mutable state. All communication is message passing (copied). This is a feature (no races) but requires a different design.",[23,1136,1138],{"id":1137},"worker-pools","Worker Pools",[14,1140,1141],{},"For many tasks, spawn a few isolates once and reuse them:",[67,1143,1144],{"language":69},[71,1145,1147],{"className":73,"code":1146,"language":69,"meta":75,"style":75},"class WorkerPool {\n    final List\u003CIsolate> _workers = [];\n    final List\u003CSendPort> _ports = [];\n\n    Future\u003Cvoid> spawn(int count) async {\n        for (var i = 0; i \u003C count; i++) {\n            final receivePort = ReceivePort();\n            final isolate = await Isolate.spawn(_workerEntry, receivePort.sendPort);\n            _workers.add(isolate);\n            _ports.add(await receivePort.first as SendPort);\n        }\n    }\n    \u002F\u002F ... send tasks to workers, collect results\n}\n",[31,1148,1149,1159,1179,1196,1200,1224,1250,1263,1283,1294,1314,1319,1324,1329],{"__ignoreMap":75},[79,1150,1151,1154,1157],{"class":81,"line":82},[79,1152,1153],{"class":106},"class",[79,1155,1156],{"class":85}," WorkerPool",[79,1158,110],{"class":89},[79,1160,1161,1163,1166,1168,1171,1174,1176],{"class":81,"line":113},[79,1162,456],{"class":106},[79,1164,1165],{"class":85}," List",[79,1167,90],{"class"