79,1292,1293],{"class":89},"(isolate);\n",[79,1295,1296,1299,1301,1303,1305,1308,1310,1312],{"class":81,"line":234},[79,1297,1298],{"class":89},"            _ports.",[79,1300,1290],{"class":99},[79,1302,403],{"class":89},[79,1304,937],{"class":106},[79,1306,1307],{"class":89}," receivePort.first ",[79,1309,705],{"class":106},[79,1311,708],{"class":85},[79,1313,425],{"class":89},[79,1315,1316],{"class":81,"line":254},[79,1317,1318],{"class":89},"        }\n",[79,1320,1321],{"class":81,"line":263},[79,1322,1323],{"class":89},"    }\n",[79,1325,1326],{"class":81,"line":499},[79,1327,1328],{"class":430},"    \u002F\u002F ... send tasks to workers, collect results\n",[79,1330,1331],{"class":81,"line":521},[79,1332,209],{"class":89},[14,1334,1335,1336,1339,1340,1343],{},"Or use a package like ",[31,1337,1338],{},"worker_manager"," or ",[31,1341,1342],{},"pool"," for managed worker pools.",[23,1345,1347],{"id":1346},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[39,1349,1350,1368,1383,1393,1403],{},[42,1351,1352,1355,1356,1358,1359,1361,1362,1365,1366,760],{},[18,1353,1354],{},"Idiom",": use ",[31,1357,59],{}," (or ",[31,1360,318],{}," in Flutter) for one-shot CPU-heavy work — ",[31,1363,1364],{},"await Isolate.run(() => heavyTask())"," offloads to a separate isolate, not blocking the main\u002FUI thread. Simpler than ",[31,1367,367],{},[42,1369,1370,1372,1373,808,1375,1377,1378,1382],{},[18,1371,1354],{},": don't use isolates for I\u002FO — ",[31,1374,86],{},[31,1376,937],{}," is sufficient (the event loop handles I\u002FO concurrency). Isolates are for ",[1379,1380,1381],"em",{},"CPU-heavy"," work (parsing, compression, image processing). Using isolates for I\u002FO adds overhead without benefit.",[42,1384,1385,1355,1387,1389,1390,1392],{},[18,1386,1354],{},[31,1388,851],{}," for large byte buffers — it transfers (zero-copy) instead of copying. For a large ",[31,1391,847],{}," between isolates, this is much faster than the default deep copy.",[42,1394,1395,1397,1398,1339,1400,1402],{},[18,1396,1354],{},": use a worker pool for many small tasks — spawning an isolate has ~50ms overhead. For many tasks, spawn a few isolates once and reuse them (send messages). Use ",[31,1399,1338],{},[31,1401,1342],{}," packages for managed pools.",[42,1404,1405,1407],{},[18,1406,1354],{},": keep isolate functions top-level or static — closures sent to isolates must be sendable. Top-level functions and static methods are safely sendable. Avoid sending closures that capture non-sendable objects.",[23,1409,1411],{"id":1410},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[39,1413,1414,1420,1429,1435,1444,1450,1471,1477,1492,1500],{},[42,1415,1416,1419],{},[18,1417,1418],{},"Spawn overhead (~50ms)",": for small tasks, the overhead exceeds the benefit. Use a worker pool (spawn once, reuse) for many small tasks.",[42,1421,1422,1425,1426,1428],{},[18,1423,1424],{},"Messages are deep-copied",": sending a large object to an isolate copies it (memory + time). Use ",[31,1427,851],{}," for large byte buffers (zero-copy).",[42,1430,1431,1434],{},[18,1432,1433],{},"Isolates don't share memory",": no shared mutable state. All communication is message passing. This is a feature (no races) but requires a different design (pass data, not share).",[42,1436,1437,1440,1441,1443],{},[18,1438,1439],{},"Web doesn't support isolates",": Dart on the web (JS) is single-threaded. ",[31,1442,59],{}," may throw or run on the main thread. Don't rely on isolates for web builds — use Web Workers (via JS interop) if needed.",[42,1445,1446,1449],{},[18,1447,1448],{},"Closures must capture sendable values",": a function sent to an isolate can capture variables, but they must be sendable (copied). Capturing a non-sendable object (e.g., a file handle) fails.",[42,1451,1452,1457,1458,1460,1461,1463,1464,1466,1467,1054,1469,122],{},[18,1453,1454,1455],{},"Errors propagate from ",[31,1456,59],{},": a thrown error in ",[31,1459,59],{}," is caught by the ",[31,1462,937],{},"er. For ",[31,1465,367],{},", handle errors via ",[31,1468,1053],{},[31,1470,1057],{},[42,1472,1473,1476],{},[18,1474,1475],{},"Isolates are not threads",": they're independent workers with their own heap. No locks, no shared memory. The actor model — message passing only.",[42,1478,1479,1484,1485,1487,1488,1491],{},[18,1480,1481,1483],{},[31,1482,535],{}," must be closed",": a ",[31,1486,535],{}," keeps the isolate alive. Close it (",[31,1489,1490],{},"receivePort.close()",") when done, or the isolate won't exit.",[42,1493,1494,1499],{},[18,1495,1496],{},[31,1497,1498],{},"Isolate.kill()",": forcibly kills an isolate. Use for cleanup, but it doesn't run finalizers. Prefer graceful shutdown (send a \"stop\" message, close ports).",[42,1501,1502,932,1505,1508],{},[18,1503,1504],{},"Named isolates",[31,1506,1507],{},"Isolate.spawn(entry, msg, debugName: 'worker-1')"," names the isolate for debugging\u002Fprofiling. Helps identify in DevTools.",[23,1510,1512],{"id":1511},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1514,1515],{},"A developer offloads file I\u002FO to an isolate, but it's slower than doing it on the main thread:",[67,1517,1518],{"language":69},[71,1519,1521],{"className":73,"code":1520,"language":69,"meta":75,"style":75},"Future\u003CString> readFile(String path) async {\n    return Isolate.run(() => File(path).readAsString());\n}\n",[31,1522,1523,1547,1573],{"__ignoreMap":75},[79,1524,1525,1527,1529,1531,1533,1536,1538,1540,1543,1545],{"class":81,"line":82},[79,1526,86],{"class":85},[79,1528,90],{"class":89},[79,1530,785],{"class":85},[79,1532,96],{"class":89},[79,1534,1535],{"class":99},"readFile",[79,1537,403],{"class":89},[79,1539,785],{"class":85},[79,1541,1542],{"class":89}," path) ",[79,1544,107],{"class":106},[79,1546,110],{"class":89},[79,1548,1549,1551,1553,1555,1557,1559,1561,1564,1567,1570],{"class":81,"line":113},[79,1550,116],{"class":106},[79,1552,119],{"class":85},[79,1554,122],{"class":89},[79,1556,125],{"class":99},[79,1558,300],{"class":89},[79,1560,303],{"class":106},[79,1562,1563],{"class":85}," File",[79,1565,1566],{"class":89},"(path).",[79,1568,1569],{"class":99},"readAsString",[79,1571,1572],{"class":89},"());\n",[79,1574,1575],{"class":81,"line":131},[79,1576,209],{"class":89},[14,1578,1579],{},"What's wrong?",[1581,1582,1583,1587,1598,1603,1650,1661,1664,1700,1703,1732],"details",{},[1584,1585,1586],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1588,1589,1590,1593,1594,1597],{},"File I\u002FO is ",[18,1591,1592],{},"I\u002FO-bound",", not CPU-bound. ",[31,1595,1596],{},"File.readAsString()"," is async — it yields to the event loop while waiting for the disk. Offloading it to an isolate adds ~50ms spawn overhead (and a message copy for the result) without benefit — the main isolate could have awaited the I\u002FO directly, with the event loop handling concurrency.",[14,1599,1600,1601,825],{},"The fix — do I\u002FO on the main isolate with ",[31,1602,937],{},[71,1604,1606],{"className":73,"code":1605,"language":69,"meta":75,"style":75},"Future\u003CString> readFile(String path) async {\n    return File(path).readAsString();   \u002F\u002F already async, event loop handles it\n}\n",[31,1607,1608,1630,1646],{"__ignoreMap":75},[79,1609,1610,1612,1614,1616,1618,1620,1622,1624,1626,1628],{"class":81,"line":82},[79,1611,86],{"class":85},[79,1613,90],{"class":89},[79,1615,785],{"class":85},[79,1617,96],{"class":89},[79,1619,1535],{"class":99},[79,1621,403],{"class":89},[79,1623,785],{"class":85},[79,1625,1542],{"class":89},[79,1627,107],{"class":106},[79,1629,110],{"class":89},[79,1631,1632,1634,1636,1638,1640,1643],{"class":81,"line":113},[79,1633,116],{"class":106},[79,1635,1563],{"class":85},[79,1637,1566],{"class":89},[79,1639,1569],{"class":99},[79,1641,1642],{"class":89},"();   ",[79,1644,1645],{"class":430},"\u002F\u002F already async, event loop handles it\n",[79,1647,1648],{"class":81,"line":131},[79,1649,209],{"class":89},[14,1651,1652,1653,1655,1656,808,1658,1660],{},"::\nIsolates are for ",[18,1654,925],{}," (parsing, compression, image processing) that would block the main isolate's event loop. For I\u002FO (file, network, timers), ",[31,1657,86],{},[31,1659,937],{}," is sufficient — the event loop handles concurrency while the I\u002FO is in progress.",[14,1662,1663],{},"Use isolates when:",[71,1665,1667],{"className":73,"code":1666,"language":69,"meta":75,"style":75},"\u002F\u002F CPU-heavy: parsing a huge JSON string\nfinal data = await Isolate.run(() => jsonDecode(hugeJsonString));\n",[31,1668,1669,1674],{"__ignoreMap":75},[79,1670,1671],{"class":81,"line":82},[79,1672,1673],{"class":430},"\u002F\u002F CPU-heavy: parsing a huge JSON string\n",[79,1675,1676,1678,1680,1682,1684,1686,1688,1690,1692,1694,1697],{"class":81,"line":113},[79,1677,285],{"class":106},[79,1679,901],{"class":89},[79,1681,140],{"class":106},[79,1683,245],{"class":106},[79,1685,119],{"class":85},[79,1687,122],{"class":89},[79,1689,125],{"class":99},[79,1691,300],{"class":89},[79,1693,303],{"class":106},[79,1695,1696],{"class":99}," jsonDecode",[79,1698,1699],{"class":89},"(hugeJsonString));\n",[14,1701,1702],{},"::\nDon't use isolates when:",[71,1704,1706],{"className":73,"code":1705,"language":69,"meta":75,"style":75},"\u002F\u002F I\u002FO-bound: reading a file (async, event loop handles it)\nfinal content = await File(path).readAsString();\n",[31,1707,1708,1713],{"__ignoreMap":75},[79,1709,1710],{"class":81,"line":82},[79,1711,1712],{"class":430},"\u002F\u002F I\u002FO-bound: reading a file (async, event loop handles it)\n",[79,1714,1715,1717,1720,1722,1724,1726,1728,1730],{"class":81,"line":113},[79,1716,285],{"class":106},[79,1718,1719],{"class":89}," content ",[79,1721,140],{"class":106},[79,1723,245],{"class":106},[79,1725,1563],{"class":85},[79,1727,1566],{"class":89},[79,1729,1569],{"class":99},[79,1731,251],{"class":89},[14,1733,1734,1735,1738],{},"::\n",[18,1736,1737],{},"The lesson",": isolates are for CPU-heavy work (blocks the event loop), not I\u002FO (which is async and handled by the event loop). Offloading I\u002FO to an isolate adds spawn overhead + copy overhead without benefit.",[23,1740,1741],{"id":1584},"Summary",[14,1743,1744,1745,1747,1748,1750,1751,1753,1754,808,1756,1758,1759,1761],{},"You understand isolates (no shared memory, message passing), ",[31,1746,59],{}," (one-shot CPU work), ",[31,1749,318],{}," (Flutter wrapper), ",[31,1752,367],{}," + ",[31,1755,535],{},[31,1757,406],{}," (long-running, bidirectional), sendable messages (deep-copied, ",[31,1760,851],{}," for zero-copy), when to use isolates (CPU-heavy, not I\u002FO), worker pools, error handling, and web limitations — with the I\u002FO-doesn't-need-isolates and spawn-overhead traps avoided. Next: error handling and exceptions.",[1763,1764,1765],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}",{"title":75,"searchDepth":113,"depth":113,"links":1767},[1768,1769,1773,1775,1779,1780,1781,1782,1783,1784,1785,1786,1787,1788,1789],{"id":25,"depth":113,"text":26},{"id":56,"depth":113,"text":1770,"children":1771},"Isolate.run (Dart 2.19+, recommended)",[1772],{"id":272,"depth":131,"text":273},{"id":315,"depth":113,"text":1774},"compute (Flutter)",{"id":364,"depth":113,"text":1776,"children":1777},"Isolate.spawn (low-level)",[1778],{"id":556,"depth":131,"text":557},{"id":763,"depth":113,"text":764},{"id":836,"depth":113,"text":837},{"id":917,"depth":113,"text":918},{"id":947,"depth":113,"text":948},{"id":1061,"depth":113,"text":1064},{"id":1110,"depth":113,"text":1111},{"id":1137,"depth":113,"text":1138},{"id":1346,"depth":113,"text":1347},{"id":1410,"depth":113,"text":1411},{"id":1511,"depth":113,"text":1512},{"id":1584,"depth":113,"text":1741},"Dart is single-threaded. For CPU-heavy work (parsing, compression, image processing), use isolates — separate threads with their own memory heap.","md",{},"\u002Fdart\u002F10-isolates-and-concurrency",{"title":5,"description":1790},"dart\u002F10-isolates-and-concurrency","Tnqwsvwmg8f_0Jtra2TpltXcLgprliTk5Dw8n4XzqwI",1787401240007]